e2c3c6443d1cefcd0ad08642122d1e31004a" commit="b3fc249c1beb64cb88970d1d55390ec0014b24b3" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/tegra: Fix the NULL edid issue  Sometimes the panel EDID can't be retrieved via dpaux, and this causes an issue that because no EDID is provided, drm falls back to a display resolution of 1024x768.  The cause of this issue is, in tegra_dpaux_transfer, it fails because of the timeout error:  if (value &amp; DPAUX_DP_AUXSTAT_TIMEOUT_ERROR) {  ret = -ETIMEDOUT;  goto out; }  And the reason for this is, dpaux doesn't get reset correctly. We're relying on powergate/unpowergate SOR power parition to reset dpaux, while SOR power partition is ref-counted.  So this patch does 2 things: - Assert/Deassert reset manually in dpaux disable/enable functions - Wait HPD in tegra_dpaux_transfer to make sure panel is ready before   any transactions  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55903 TEST=The 1024x768 doesn't happen again  Change-Id: I1fd3e2c3c6443d1cefcd0ad08642122d1e31004a Signed-off-by: Mark Zhang &lt;markz@gpartner-nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/366650 Tested-by: Vince Hsu &lt;vince.h@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="366650" owner_email="markz@gpartner-nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/366650/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="8728.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>